<BaseLayout title="Power Steering" description="Hydraulic power steering adapters, pressure reducer, and electric power steering for LS Genesis Coupe swaps.">
  <h1>Power Steering</h1>
  <div class="note"><p><strong>Use Pentosin CHF 202 synthetic hydraulic fluid.</strong></p></div>

  <h2>Hydraulic (GM Pump)</h2>
  <h3>High-Pressure Line Adapter</h3>
  <p>
    If you're not getting the Sikky PS lines kit, you'll need an adapter for the high-pressure PS line that ends near the front subframe.
    Don't cheap out — other adapters have been tried and leak. Or mount directly to the rack with the fitting below.
  </p>
  <h3>Pressure Reducer</h3>
  <p>
    The GM pump puts out about <strong>1200 psi</strong>; the Genesis rack needs about <strong>850 psi</strong>. Use a pressure reducer kit with 2 or 3 of the supplied shims.
    Some have gotten away without shims, so this is debatable.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://www.summitracing.com/parts/krs-krc10122000" target="_blank" rel="noopener">KRC pressure reducer kit (Summit KRS-KRC10122000)</a></li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Rack Fitting</h3>
  <p>Or use this to adapt directly to the PS rack if you don't get the full Sikky kit:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="https://www.summitracing.com/parts/rus-648060" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Russell 648060</a> —
      AN to metric adapter fitting, straight, aluminum, -6 AN to 16mm x 1.5 O-ring.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Electric Power Steering</h2>
  <p>By Alex Toothman on the Genesis Coupe LS Swaps Facebook page.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Video: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/share/v/185cA96S7q/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Facebook</a></li>
    <li>CAN bus controller, -6AN adapter block, and empty connectors: <a href="https://reformmotorsports.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reform Motorsports</a></li>
    <li>Reservoir if you buy a Jeep/Durango pump: <a href="https://a.co/d/02RjfRzP" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Amazon</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p><em>Wiring diagram and pump-mount photos are in the original Google Doc — send them over and they'll be added here.</em></p>

  <CommunityLinks />
</BaseLayout>
